course: dictionary
lesson: 7011
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word parent is a good example. Every child has two parents, a mother and a father, but other words for parent are also used for any adult who looks after a child.
explain: «Any secret someone asks you to keep from your parents is a reason to tell them.» Here parents means the adults who bring you up. To check, swap in a meaning of your own, such as "the adults who look after me", and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Parent can also be a verb, meaning to bring up and look after a child. Parent can be used with animals and plants too: a parent animal or plant is one that has young. Read the words around the word to see which meaning fits.
fact: A parent is a mother or a father.
fact: A parent is also any adult who brings up a child, like a step-parent or a foster parent.
fact: To parent means to bring up and look after a child.
fact: A parent animal or plant is one that has young, and young animals and plants get features from their parents.
fact: «Parents and carers» means the adults who look after children, and «single parent» means one parent bringing up a child alone.
exercise: «Any secret someone asks you to keep from your parents is a reason to tell them.» In this sentence, what does parents mean? | The rules of a board game | *The adults who bring you up | Sweets you are allowed for a treat | Two shops in the town centre
exercise: «Borrowing books from the public library is free, and a parent can help you get your own library card.» What is a parent in this sentence? | A kind of library shelf | A book about dinosaurs | *An adult who looks after a child | A card that opens doors
exercise: Ella says a plant can be a parent. What does parent mean for a plant? | A plant that has no roots | A plant that grows in a pot | *A plant that has young | A plant with yellow leaves
test: «Older children in big families often help a lot, but if it gets too much, tell a parent or a teacher.» In this sentence, parent is a noun. Which meaning fits? | A loud noise in the playground | A game played with cards | *An adult who looks after a child | A tool for cutting paper
test: A child has two parents, a mother and a father. How many parents does a child usually have? | *2 | 1 | 4 | 3
exam: «Parents, teachers and youth workers are trusted adults who can help.» What does parents mean here? | Fast runners in a race | *Mothers, fathers or other adults who look after a child | A kind of school bell | Wooden toys for young children
